    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Available now.\n\nGet let are delighted to present this exceptional one bedroom city centre apartment to the market. 18 Lower Baggot street is a hugely impressive and beautiful residential development which boasts spacious and light-filled accommodation. This apartment is located on the ground floor of this Baggot Street development and overlooks Fitzwilliam Lane. The well-proportioned accommodation offers stylish functionality throughout. The apartments furnishings and contemporary interior give the accommodation a high sense of comfort and homeliness. Residents can also enjoy use of the stunning communal roof garden as well as a peaceful communal lounge / study area. \n\nThe internal layout benefits greatly from its open planned, sophisticated nature. The living and dining area are joined to the modern kitchen and entrance hallway. A floor to ceiling glass wall creates a sense of division while maintaining the flow of the room. The luxurious kitchen is fitted with top of the range appliances. Accessing into the living quarters you also have space for a dining area in the light filled room. The living area is furnished to a high standard and has build in bookshelves. This tastefully decorated room is the focal point of the apartment. The double bedroom is carpeted and has a large built in double wardrobe boasting ample storage space. The bathroom is adjacent to the bedroom. The bathroom is tiled floor to ceiling and is fitted with a walk in shower and large medicine cabinets. Please note there is no parking space available with this property. \n\nBaggot Street is a highly enviable and particularly sought after area of Dublin 2. The convenient city centre location is within walking distance of the city\\`s business district around Merrion and Fitzwilliam St and the technology hub of Grand Canal, where Facebook, Google, Air BnB and all have their EMEA headquarters. Within a short stroll is a selection of top class restaurants, cafes and shopping facilities and Dublin`s main shopping thoroughfare around Grafton St is a short stroll. \n\nTo arrange a viewing please email Diana Farkas of Get Let by clicking on the Email Advertiser link to the right of this page, ideally submitting a brief application outlining times available to view, etc. Private viewings shall then take place by appointment only. Get Let is a subsidiary of Get Property Limited, PSRA number 002324."
